  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of emergency life-saving Health, Child Protection and WASH services to communities affected by the recent conflict in Myanmar during the fourth quarter of 2023.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this UNICE project is to improve access to essential health care services, protection support, and WASH services and supplies for children, women, and their families. This project provides the supply of essential medicines and equipment for emergency primary health care including maternal, and newborn, as well as the provision of healthcare services to women, children, and families through mobile teams and community health workers, amongst other activities. The Protection component of this project will provide assistance to 15,000 people including 3,500 women and 9,000 children and including 700 persons with disabilities. The Health component of this project will provide assistance to 30,000 people, including 7,500 women 18,000 children and including 2,400 persons with disabilities. The Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) component of this project will provide assistance to 40,000 people including 14,000 women and 13,000 children and including 2,000 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
